<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Molossians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Molossians were the leading tribe of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>, in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dodona">Dodona</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ioannina">Ioannina</a> basin. Ruled by the Aeacid kings, who claimed descent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achilles">Achilles</a>, they united the Epirote tribes under their leadership and produced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olympia">Olympias</a> and Pyrrhus. In 167 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> sold 150,000 Epirotes into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>, devastating their land.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/molossians.jpg" alt="Molossians" width="320" height="305" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Megistias · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Epirus_antiquus_tabula.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
